    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\nI implemented the public-holiday extension to the business-day rule in `Owner.resolveRegistrationDate` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`):\n\n- Replaced the single-step weekend `switch` with an iterative roll-forward that advances one day at a time until the date lands on a non-holiday business day. This correctly handles chained cases (e.g. a holiday rolling onto a weekend, or consecutive holidays like 2026-12-25 \u2192 2026-12-28).\n- Added a fixed `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28) and an `isBusinessDay` helper that excludes Saturdays, Sundays, and those holidays.\n\nThe full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).",
