    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension that fits the existing structure:\n\n- It builds directly on the `resolveRegistrationDate` method that already lived in `Owner`, so the holiday rule lands exactly where the weekend rule already was \u2014 no new home needed, no logic scattered.\n- The weekend `switch` is replaced by a single `while (!isBusinessDay(effective))` loop, which generalizes cleanly to \"roll past weekends *and* holidays\" without duplicating the roll logic. The old special-casing of Saturday/Sunday offsets is gone, so there's one coherent advance-until-business-day rule rather than two parallel notions.\n- `isBusinessDay` is a well-scoped private helper that names the concept, and `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` is a `private static final Set` \u2014 the idiomatic way to express a fixed lookup list. The constant sits adjacent to its sole consumer, which keeps the holiday rule self-contained.\n- The Javadoc was updated to match the new behavior, including the `@return` contract, so the documentation stays coherent with the code.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class or method is becoming a catch-all, and a Spring/Java maintainer would find this natural.",
